/-!
# The Brauer algebra acting on a tensor power of the standard symplectic module

Equip `V = R^{2n} = (Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R` with its standard alternating bilinear form, represented
by `Matrix.J (Fin n) R`, whose inverse copairing has matrix `-J`. A Brauer diagram `D` on `k`
strands acts on the tensor power `V^{⊗k}`: its through strands carry tensor slots from bottom to
top with the sign twist forced by the alternating form, its caps contract two input slots against
`J`, and its cups insert `-J` into two output slots.

Because `J` is skew-symmetric and a through strand oriented from top to bottom negates the
Kronecker delta of one oriented from bottom to top, the local pair weight
`TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.symplecticArcWeight` on the boundary points of `D` is skew-symmetric. In the
monomial basis `TauCeti.symplecticTensorPowerBasis`, the entry of the matrix
`TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix` at output labelling `v` and input labelling `u` is
therefore the Pfaffian-signed product `D.signedWeight (symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v))`
developed in `TauCeti/Combinatorics/Brauer/SignedWeight.lean`.

These matrices multiply by the loop rule of the Brauer algebra at the **negative** loop value
`δ = -2|l|` (`TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix_mul`): stacking a cap-cup generator
above a diagram either closes up an existing cup into a loop contributing `-tr(J * Jᵀ) = -2|l|`, or
reconnects two distinct arcs where the matrix identity `J² = -1` supplies the minus sign matching
the transposition parity of reconnection (`TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.signedWeight_reconnect`). Induction
along `TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.capCup_induction_on` together with weighted associativity extends this
to arbitrary diagrams, assembling the operators into an algebra homomorphism
`TauCeti.brauerActionSymp` from `B_k(-2n)` to `Module.End R (V^{⊗k})`.

On a permutation diagram `permToBrauer σ`, `brauerActionSymp` agrees with the sign-twisted
permutation action `TauCeti.symplecticPermTensorAction`
(`TauCeti.brauerActionSymp_of_permToBrauer`), and on a cap-cup diagram `capCup a b` (`a ≠ b`) it
agrees with the single-arc operator `TauCeti.symplecticCupCapAt`
(`TauCeti.brauerActionSymp_of_capCup`).

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.symplecticArcWeight`: the skew-symmetric pair weight on `Fin k ⊕ Fin k`
  associated to a boundary labelling into `l ⊕ l`.
* `TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix`: the matrix of a Brauer diagram acting on the
  `k`-th tensor power of `(l ⊕ l) → R` in the monomial basis.
* `TauCeti.symplecticTensorPowerBasis`: the monomial basis of `((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)^{⊗k}`.
* `TauCeti.symplecticPermTensorActionAlgHom`: the group-algebra extension of
  `TauCeti.symplecticPermTensorAction`.
* `TauCeti.brauerActionSymp`: the algebra homomorphism `B_k(-2n) →ₐ[R] End_R((R^{2n})^{⊗k})`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix_mul`: **the symplectic loop rule for diagram
  matrices**, `M(D₁) * M(D₂) = (-2|l|) ^ c • M(D₁ ∘ D₂)` with `c = middleLoopCount D₁ D₂`.
* `TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.transpose_symplecticActionMatrix` and
  `TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.conjTranspose_symplecticActionMatrix`: reflecting a diagram transposes
  (and conjugate-transposes) its symplectic action matrix.
* `TauCeti.toMatrix_brauerActionSymp` and `TauCeti.brauerActionSymp_of_symplecticTensorPowerBasis`:
  matrix and monomial-basis expansion of `brauerActionSymp`.
* `TauCeti.brauerActionSymp_of_permToBrauer`, `TauCeti.brauerActionSymp_comp_ofPerm` and
  `TauCeti.brauerActionSymp_of_capCup`: compatibility with the sign-twisted permutation action and
  the single-arc generators.
* `TauCeti.range_brauerActionSymp_eq_adjoin`: the image of `B_k(-2n)` is generated by the
  sign-twisted permutations and a single symplectic cap-cup operator.

## References

* [R. Brauer, *On algebras which are connected with the semisimple continuous groups*][brauer1937],
  Annals of Mathematics 38 (1937), 857-872.
* W. P. Brown, *The semisimplicity of `ω_f^n`*, Annals of Mathematics 63 (1956), 324-335.
* R. Goodman and N. R. Wallach, *Symmetry, Representations, and Invariants*, Springer GTM 255
  (2009), §10.1.
* S. Dipper, S. Doty and J. Hu, *Brauer algebras, symplectic Schur algebras and Schur-Weyl duality*,
  Transactions of the American Mathematical Society 360 (2008), 189-213.
-/

public section

open scoped Matrix TensorProduct

namespace TauCeti

universe u

namespace BrauerDiagram

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (l : Type*) [DecidableEq l] {k : ℕ}

/-! ### The skew-symmetric pair weight and diagram matrix -/

/-- **The local symplectic arc weight** on the boundary points of a `k`-strand Brauer diagram for a
boundary labelling `ℓ : (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → l ⊕ l`: horizontal arcs on either boundary read
`Matrix.J`, through strands oriented from bottom (`Sum.inl`) to top (`Sum.inr`) carry the Kronecker
delta, and through strands oriented from top to bottom carry minus the Kronecker delta so that the
weight is skew-symmetric (`TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.symplecticArcWeight_swap`). -/
def symplecticArcWeight (ℓ : (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → l ⊕ l) :
    (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → R
  | Sum.inl i, Sum.inl j => Matrix.J l R (ℓ (Sum.inl i)) (ℓ (Sum.inl j))
  | Sum.inl i, Sum.inr j => if ℓ (Sum.inl i) = ℓ (Sum.inr j) then 1 else 0
  | Sum.inr i, Sum.inl j => if ℓ (Sum.inr i) = ℓ (Sum.inl j) then -1 else 0
  | Sum.inr i, Sum.inr j => Matrix.J l R (ℓ (Sum.inr i)) (ℓ (Sum.inr j))

@[simp]
theorem symplecticArcWeight_inl_inl (ℓ : (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → l ⊕ l) (i j : Fin k) :
    symplecticArcWeight R l ℓ (Sum.inl i) (Sum.inl j) =
      Matrix.J l R (ℓ (Sum.inl i)) (ℓ (Sum.inl j)) :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem symplecticArcWeight_inl_inr (ℓ : (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → l ⊕ l) (i j : Fin k) :
    symplecticArcWeight R l ℓ (Sum.inl i) (Sum.inr j) =
      if ℓ (Sum.inl i) = ℓ (Sum.inr j) then 1 else 0 :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem symplecticArcWeight_inr_inl (ℓ : (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → l ⊕ l) (i j : Fin k) :
    symplecticArcWeight R l ℓ (Sum.inr i) (Sum.inl j) =
      if ℓ (Sum.inr i) = ℓ (Sum.inl j) then -1 else 0 :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem symplecticArcWeight_inr_inr (ℓ : (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → l ⊕ l) (i j : Fin k) :
    symplecticArcWeight R l ℓ (Sum.inr i) (Sum.inr j) =
      Matrix.J l R (ℓ (Sum.inr i)) (ℓ (Sum.inr j)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- **Skew-symmetry of the symplectic arc weight.** -/
theorem symplecticArcWeight_swap (ℓ : (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → l ⊕ l) (x y : Fin k ⊕ Fin k) :
    symplecticArcWeight R l ℓ y x = -symplecticArcWeight R l ℓ x y := by
  rcases x with i | i <;> rcases y with j | j
  · exact Matrix.J_apply_swap l R _ _
  · by_cases h : ℓ (Sum.inl i) = ℓ (Sum.inr j)
    · simp [h]
    · simp [h, Ne.symm h]
  · by_cases h : ℓ (Sum.inr i) = ℓ (Sum.inl j)
    · simp [h]
    · simp [h, Ne.symm h]
  · exact Matrix.J_apply_swap l R _ _

/-- If two boundary labellings agree at `x` and at `y`, they assign the same symplectic arc weight
to `(x, y)`. -/
theorem symplecticArcWeight_congr {ℓ ℓ' : (Fin k ⊕ Fin k) → l ⊕ l} {x y : Fin k ⊕ Fin k}
    (hx : ℓ x = ℓ' x) (hy : ℓ y = ℓ' y) :
    symplecticArcWeight R l ℓ x y = symplecticArcWeight R l ℓ' x y := by
  rcases x with i | i <;> rcases y with j | j <;> simp_all

/-- **The matrix of a Brauer diagram** acting on the `k`-th tensor power of `(l ⊕ l) → R` with its
standard alternating form, in the monomial basis indexed by `Fin k → l ⊕ l`: the entry at output
labelling `v` and input labelling `u` is the Pfaffian-signed arc weight of `Sum.elim u v`. -/
def symplecticActionMatrix (D : BrauerDiagram k) :
    Matrix (Fin k → l ⊕ l) (Fin k → l ⊕ l) R :=
  Matrix.of fun v u => D.signedWeight (symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v))

@[simp]
theorem symplecticActionMatrix_apply (D : BrauerDiagram k) (v u : Fin k → l ⊕ l) :
    D.symplecticActionMatrix R l v u =
      D.signedWeight (symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The identity diagram has the identity matrix. -/
@[simp]
theorem symplecticActionMatrix_permToBrauer_one :
    (permToBrauer 1).symplecticActionMatrix R l =
      (1 : Matrix (Fin k → l ⊕ l) (Fin k → l ⊕ l) R) := by
  ext v u
  rw [symplecticActionMatrix_apply, signedWeight_permToBrauer_one, Matrix.one_apply]
  split_ifs with h
  · subst h; simp
  · obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := Function.ne_iff.mp h
    exact Finset.prod_eq_zero (Finset.mem_univ r) (by simp [hr.symm])

/-- **The matrix entries of a permutation diagram**: `(permToBrauer σ)` has entry `sign σ` where
`v = u ∘ σ.symm` and `0` elsewhere. -/
theorem symplecticActionMatrix_permToBrauer (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin k)) (v u : Fin k → l ⊕ l) :
    (permToBrauer σ).symplecticActionMatrix R l v u =
      if v = fun i => u (σ.symm i) then ((Equiv.Perm.sign σ : ℤ) : R) else 0 := by
  rw [symplecticActionMatrix_apply, signedWeight_permToBrauer (symplecticArcWeight_swap R l _)]
  split_ifs with hv
  · subst hv; simp
  · obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := Function.ne_iff.mp hv
    rw [Finset.prod_eq_zero (Finset.mem_univ (σ.symm j)) (by simp [hj.symm]), smul_zero]

/-- **The matrix entries of a cap-cup diagram** on distinct strands `a ≠ b`: `-(J (u a) (u b) *
J (v a) (v b))` when `v` agrees with `u` off `{a, b}`, and `0` otherwise, matching
`TauCeti.piTensorProduct_repr_symplecticCupCapAt_piTensorProduct`. -/
theorem symplecticActionMatrix_capCup {a b : Fin k} (hab : a ≠ b) (v u : Fin k → l ⊕ l) :
    (capCup a b).symplecticActionMatrix R l v u =
      if ∀ r, r ≠ a → r ≠ b → v r = u r then
        -(Matrix.J l R (u a) (u b) * Matrix.J l R (v a) (v b))
      else 0 := by
  rw [symplecticActionMatrix_apply, signedWeight_capCup (symplecticArcWeight_swap R l _) hab]
  split_ifs with h
  · rw [Finset.prod_eq_one fun r hr => by
      obtain ⟨hrb, hra⟩ := Finset.mem_erase.mp hr
      simp [h r (Finset.mem_erase.mp hra).1 hrb]]
    simp
  · push Not at h
    obtain ⟨r, hra, hrb, hvu⟩ := h
    have hr : r ∈ ((Finset.univ : Finset (Fin k)).erase a).erase b :=
      Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨hrb, Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨hra, Finset.mem_univ r⟩⟩
    rw [Finset.prod_eq_zero hr (by simp [hvu.symm]), mul_zero, neg_zero]

/-! ### Transpose and conjugate transpose -/

private theorem symplecticArcWeight_swap_points (v u : Fin k → l ⊕ l) (x y : Fin k ⊕ Fin k) :
    symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v) x.swap y.swap =
      (if x.isLeft then -1 else 1) * (if y.isLeft then -1 else 1) *
        symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim v u) x y := by
  rcases x with i | i <;> rcases y with j | j
  · simp
  · by_cases h : v i = u j <;> simp [h]
  · by_cases h : u i = v j <;> simp [h]
  · simp

/-- **Reflecting a diagram transposes its symplectic action matrix**: exchanging bottom and top
points flips the sign of each bottom endpoint in `symplecticArcWeight`, contributing `(-1) ^ k` over
all `2 * k` endpoints, which cancels the reflection parity `(-1) ^ k` from
`TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.signedWeight_flip`. -/
@[simp]
theorem transpose_symplecticActionMatrix (D : BrauerDiagram k) :
    (D.symplecticActionMatrix R l)ᵀ = D.flip.symplecticActionMatrix R l := by
  ext v u
  let ε : Fin k ⊕ Fin k → R := fun z => if z.isLeft then -1 else 1
  have hε : (∏ r : Fin k, ε (D.arcPerm (Sum.inl r)) * ε (D.arcPerm (Sum.inr r))) =
      (-1 : R) ^ k := by
    rw [Finset.prod_mul_distrib,
      ← Fintype.prod_sum_type fun z => ε (D.arcPerm z),
      Equiv.prod_comp D.arcPerm ε, Fintype.prod_sum_type]
    simp [ε]
  rw [Matrix.transpose_apply, symplecticActionMatrix_apply, symplecticActionMatrix_apply,
    signedWeight_flip (symplecticArcWeight_swap R l _), signedWeight_def, signedWeight_def]
  have hterm (r : Fin k) :
      symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v)
          (D.arcPerm (Sum.inl r)).swap (D.arcPerm (Sum.inr r)).swap =
        (ε (D.arcPerm (Sum.inl r)) * ε (D.arcPerm (Sum.inr r))) *
          symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim v u)
            (D.arcPerm (Sum.inl r)) (D.arcPerm (Sum.inr r)) := by
    simpa only [ε, mul_assoc] using
      symplecticArcWeight_swap_points R l v u (D.arcPerm (Sum.inl r)) (D.arcPerm (Sum.inr r))
  rw [Finset.prod_congr rfl fun r _ => hterm r, Finset.prod_mul_distrib, hε, mul_smul_comm,
    ← mul_assoc, ← mul_pow, neg_one_mul, neg_neg, one_pow, one_mul]

/-- Every entry of `symplecticActionMatrix` is an integer (`0` or `±1`), so over any star ring its
conjugate transpose agrees with its transpose, the matrix of `D.flip`. -/
@[simp]
theorem conjTranspose_symplecticActionMatrix [StarRing R] (D : BrauerDiagram k) :
    (D.symplecticActionMatrix R l)ᴴ = D.flip.symplecticActionMatrix R l := by
  rw [← transpose_symplecticActionMatrix]
  ext v u
  rw [Matrix.conjTranspose_apply, Matrix.transpose_apply, symplecticActionMatrix_apply,
    ← starRingEnd_apply, map_signedWeight]
  refine signedWeight_congr_arcs D fun x _ => ?_
  rw [starRingEnd_apply]
  have hstarJ (p q : l ⊕ l) : star (Matrix.J l R p q) = Matrix.J l R p q := by
    rcases p with a | a <;> rcases q with b | b <;>
      { by_cases h : a = b <;> simp [Matrix.J, h] }
  rcases x with i | i <;> rcases D.val _ with j | j
  · exact hstarJ _ _
  · by_cases h : v i = u j <;> simp [h]
  · by_cases h : u i = v j <;> simp [h]
  · exact hstarJ _ _

/-! ### Matrix multiplication and the loop rule -/

section Mul

variable [Fintype l]

/-- Multiplying on the left by a permutation diagram relabels the top boundary and scales by
`sign σ`, with no middle loops formed. -/
private theorem symplecticActionMatrix_permToBrauer_mul (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin k))
    (D : BrauerDiagram k) :
    (permToBrauer σ).symplecticActionMatrix R l * D.symplecticActionMatrix R l =
      (composeDiagram (permToBrauer σ) D).symplecticActionMatrix R l := by
  ext v u
  rw [Matrix.mul_apply, Finset.sum_eq_single (v ∘ σ)]
  · have hv : v = fun i => (v ∘ σ) (σ.symm i) := by ext i; simp
    rw [symplecticActionMatrix_permToBrauer, if_congr (iff_of_true hv trivial) rfl rfl, ite_true,
      symplecticActionMatrix_apply, composeDiagram_permToBrauer_left, symplecticActionMatrix_apply,
      relabel_def, signedWeight_congr (symplecticArcWeight_swap R l _), Equiv.Perm.sign_sumCongr,
      map_one, one_mul, zsmul_eq_mul]
    refine congrArg _ (signedWeight_congr_arcs D fun x _ => ?_)
    rcases x with i | i <;> rcases D.val _ with j | j
    · simp [Equiv.Perm.one_def]
    · by_cases h : u i = v (σ j) <;> simp [Equiv.Perm.one_def, h]
    · by_cases h : v (σ i) = u j <;> simp [Equiv.Perm.one_def, h]
    · simp [Equiv.Perm.one_def]
  · intro m _ hm
    have hvm : v ≠ fun i => m (σ.symm i) := by
      rintro rfl
      exact hm (by ext i; simp)
    rw [symplecticActionMatrix_permToBrauer]
    simp [hvm]
  · simp

/-- Multiplying any vector `f` by the `v`-row of `(capCup a b).symplecticActionMatrix` sums over
the `l ⊕ l` label pairs `(x, y)` on the strands `a` and `b`. -/
private theorem sum_capCup_mul_eq {a b : Fin k} (hab : a ≠ b) (v : Fin k → l ⊕ l)
    (f : (Fin k → l ⊕ l) → R) :
    ∑ m : Fin k → l ⊕ l, (capCup a b).symplecticActionMatrix R l v m * f m =
      -Matrix.J l R (v a) (v b) *
        ∑ x : l ⊕ l, ∑ y : l ⊕ l,
          Matrix.J l R x y * f (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y) := by
  have hupd (m : Fin k → l ⊕ l) (hm : ∀ r, r ≠ a → r ≠ b → v r = m r) :
      Function.update (Function.update v a (m a)) b (m b) = m := by
    ext r
    rcases eq_or_ne r b with rfl | hrb
    · simp
    rcases eq_or_ne r a with rfl | hra
    · simp [hab]
    · simp [hra, hrb, hm r hra hrb]
  simp_rw [symplecticActionMatrix_capCup R l hab v, ite_mul, zero_mul, ← Finset.sum_filter,
    Finset.mul_sum]
  rw [← Fintype.sum_prod_type']
  refine Finset.sum_nbij' (fun m => (m a, m b))
    (fun p => Function.update (Function.update v a p.1) b p.2) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · intro m _; exact Finset.mem_univ _
  · rintro ⟨x, y⟩ _
    refine Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, fun r hra hrb => ?_⟩
    simp [hra, hrb]
  · intro m hm
    exact hupd m (Finset.mem_filter.mp hm).2
  · rintro ⟨x, y⟩ _
    simp [hab]
  · intro m hm
    rw [hupd m (Finset.mem_filter.mp hm).2]
    ring

omit [DecidableEq l] [Fintype l] in
private theorem sum_elim_update_inr_of_ne [DecidableEq (Fin k)] {a b : Fin k}
    (u v : Fin k → l ⊕ l) (x y : l ⊕ l) {z : Fin k ⊕ Fin k}
    (hza : z ≠ Sum.inr a) (hzb : z ≠ Sum.inr b) :
    Sum.elim u (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y) z = Sum.elim u v z := by
  rcases z with i | j
  · rfl
  · have hja : j ≠ a := by simpa using hza
    have hjb : j ≠ b := by simpa using hzb
    simp [hja, hjb]

private theorem sum_J_mul_ite_mul_J (p q : l ⊕ l) :
    ∑ x : l ⊕ l, ∑ y : l ⊕ l,
        Matrix.J l R x y * (if x = p then (-1 : R) else 0) * Matrix.J l R y q =
      if p = q then 1 else 0 := by
  have hinner (x : l ⊕ l) :
      (∑ y : l ⊕ l, Matrix.J l R x y * (if x = p then (-1 : R) else 0) * Matrix.J l R y q) =
        if x = p then -(Matrix.J l R * Matrix.J l R) p q else 0 := by
    split_ifs with hx
    · subst hx
      rw [Matrix.mul_apply, ← Finset.sum_neg_distrib]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => by ring
    · simp
  simp_rw [hinner, Finset.sum_ite_eq']
  simp only [Finset.mem_univ, ite_true, Matrix.J_squared, Matrix.neg_apply, neg_neg,
    Matrix.one_apply]

private theorem sum_J_mul_J_mul_ite (p q : l ⊕ l) :
    ∑ x : l ⊕ l, ∑ y : l ⊕ l,
        Matrix.J l R x y * Matrix.J l R x p * (if y = q then (-1 : R) else 0) =
      if p = q then -1 else 0 := by
  have hinner (x : l ⊕ l) :
      (∑ y : l ⊕ l, Matrix.J l R x y * Matrix.J l R x p * (if y = q then (-1 : R) else 0)) =
        -(Matrix.J l R x q * Matrix.J l R x p) := by
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single q]
    · simp [mul_comm]
    · intro y _ hy; simp [hy]
    · simp
  simp_rw [hinner, Finset.sum_neg_distrib, Matrix.sum_J_mul_J_eq_ite]
  by_cases h : p = q
  · simp [h]
  · simp [h, Ne.symm h]

/-- **Two-arc contraction identity.** When `p` and `q` lie outside `{Sum.inr a, Sum.inr b}`,
contracting the arc weights at `(Sum.inr a, p)` and `(Sum.inr b, q)` against `Matrix.J` produces the
direct arc weight `symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v) p q`. -/
private theorem sum_J_mul_symplecticArcWeight_mul {a b : Fin k} (hab : a ≠ b)
    (v u : Fin k → l ⊕ l) {p q : Fin k ⊕ Fin k}
    (hpa : p ≠ Sum.inr a) (hpb : p ≠ Sum.inr b) (hqa : q ≠ Sum.inr a) (hqb : q ≠ Sum.inr b) :
    ∑ x : l ⊕ l, ∑ y : l ⊕ l,
        Matrix.J l R x y *
          symplecticArcWeight R l
            (Sum.elim u (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y)) (Sum.inr a) p *
          symplecticArcWeight R l
            (Sum.elim u (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y)) (Sum.inr b) q =
      symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v) p q := by
  rcases p with i | j <;> rcases q with i' | j'
  · simp only [symplecticArcWeight_inr_inl, symplecticArcWeight_inl_inl, Sum.elim_inl,
      Sum.elim_inr, Function.update_of_ne hab, Function.update_self]
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single (u i)]
    · rw [Finset.sum_eq_single (u i')]
      · simp
      · intro y _ hy; simp [hy]
      · simp
    · intro x _ hx; simp [hx]
    · simp
  · have hja : j' ≠ a := by simpa using hqa
    have hjb : j' ≠ b := by simpa using hqb
    simp only [symplecticArcWeight_inr_inl, symplecticArcWeight_inr_inr,
      symplecticArcWeight_inl_inr, Sum.elim_inl, Sum.elim_inr, Function.update_of_ne hab,
      Function.update_self, Function.update_of_ne hjb, Function.update_of_ne hja]
    exact sum_J_mul_ite_mul_J R l (u i) (v j')
  · have hja : j ≠ a := by simpa using hpa
    have hjb : j ≠ b := by simpa using hpb
    simp only [symplecticArcWeight_inr_inr, symplecticArcWeight_inr_inl, Sum.elim_inl, Sum.elim_inr,
      Function.update_of_ne hab, Function.update_self, Function.update_of_ne hjb,
      Function.update_of_ne hja]
    exact sum_J_mul_J_mul_ite R l (v j) (u i')
  · have hja : j ≠ a := by simpa using hpa
    have hjb : j ≠ b := by simpa using hpb
    have hj'a : j' ≠ a := by simpa using hqa
    have hj'b : j' ≠ b := by simpa using hqb
    simp only [symplecticArcWeight_inr_inr, Sum.elim_inr, Function.update_of_ne hab,
      Function.update_self, Function.update_of_ne hjb, Function.update_of_ne hja,
      Function.update_of_ne hj'b, Function.update_of_ne hj'a]
    calc ∑ x : l ⊕ l, ∑ y : l ⊕ l,
          Matrix.J l R x y * Matrix.J l R x (v j) * Matrix.J l R y (v j')
        = ∑ y : l ⊕ l, (∑ x : l ⊕ l, Matrix.J l R x y * Matrix.J l R x (v j)) *
            Matrix.J l R y (v j') := by
          rw [Finset.sum_comm]
          exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => by rw [Finset.sum_mul]
      _ = Matrix.J l R (v j) (v j') := by
          simp_rw [Matrix.sum_J_mul_J_eq_ite]
          simp

/-- When `D` already cups `a` to `b`, multiplying `(capCup a b).symplecticActionMatrix` by
`D.symplecticActionMatrix` scales `D.symplecticActionMatrix` by the closed-loop trace
`-(2 * Fintype.card l)`. -/
private theorem symplecticActionMatrix_capCup_mul_of_cup {a b : Fin k} (hab : a ≠ b)
    {D : BrauerDiagram k} (hcup : D.val (Sum.inr a) = Sum.inr b) (v u : Fin k → l ⊕ l) :
    ((capCup a b).symplecticActionMatrix R l * D.symplecticActionMatrix R l) v u =
      -(2 * Fintype.card l : R) * D.symplecticActionMatrix R l v u := by
  obtain ⟨r₀, π, hD, ha₀, hb₀⟩ := exists_congr_permToBrauer_one_of_point D (Sum.inr a)
  rw [hcup] at hb₀
  set W₀ := symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v)
  set P : R := ∏ r ∈ Finset.univ.erase r₀, W₀ (π (Sum.inl r)) (π (Sum.inr r))
  have hrest (x y : l ⊕ l) :
      D.signedWeight
        (symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y))) =
        (Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) • (Matrix.J l R x y * P) := by
    rw [signedWeight_eq_of_congr_permToBrauer_one (symplecticArcWeight_swap R l _) hD,
      ← Finset.mul_prod_erase Finset.univ _ (Finset.mem_univ r₀), ha₀, hb₀]
    simp only [symplecticArcWeight_inr_inr, Sum.elim_inr, Function.update_of_ne hab,
      Function.update_self]
    refine congrArg ((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) • (Matrix.J l R x y * ·))
      (Finset.prod_congr rfl fun r hr => ?_)
    have hr₀ : r ≠ r₀ := (Finset.mem_erase.mp hr).1
    exact symplecticArcWeight_congr R l
      (sum_elim_update_inr_of_ne l u v x y
        (fun h => Sum.inl_injective.ne hr₀ (π.injective (h.trans ha₀.symm)))
        (fun h => Sum.inl_ne_inr (π.injective (h.trans hb₀.symm))))
      (sum_elim_update_inr_of_ne l u v x y
        (fun h => Sum.inr_ne_inl (π.injective (h.trans ha₀.symm)))
        (fun h => Sum.inr_injective.ne hr₀ (π.injective (h.trans hb₀.symm))))
  have hD₀ : D.signedWeight W₀ =
      (Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) • (Matrix.J l R (v a) (v b) * P) := by
    simpa [W₀, Function.update_eq_self] using hrest (v a) (v b)
  rw [Matrix.mul_apply, sum_capCup_mul_eq R l hab]
  simp_rw [symplecticActionMatrix_apply, hrest, zsmul_eq_mul]
  have hsum : (∑ x : l ⊕ l, ∑ y : l ⊕ l,
      Matrix.J l R x y * (((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) : R) * (Matrix.J l R x y * P))) =
      (2 * Fintype.card l : R) * (((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) : R) * P) := by
    calc _ = (∑ x : l ⊕ l, ∑ y : l ⊕ l, Matrix.J l R x y * Matrix.J l R x y) *
          (((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) : R) * P) := by
          rw [Finset.sum_mul]
          refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => ?_
          rw [Finset.sum_mul]
          exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => by ring
      _ = _ := by rw [Matrix.sum_sum_J_mul_J]
  rw [hsum, hD₀, zsmul_eq_mul]
  ring

omit [Fintype l] in
/-- Expressing the reconnected diagram's matrix entry along a transporting permutation `π` that
places the two arcs `(Sum.inr a, p)` and `(Sum.inr b, q)` at `r₁ ≠ r₂`. -/
private theorem symplecticActionMatrix_reconnect_inr_eq {a b : Fin k} (hab : a ≠ b)
    {D : BrauerDiagram k} (hcup : D.val (Sum.inr a) ≠ Sum.inr b)
    {r₁ r₂ : Fin k} {π : Equiv.Perm (Fin k ⊕ Fin k)} (hr : r₁ ≠ r₂)
    (hD : PerfectMatching.congr π (permToBrauer 1) = D)
    (ha₁ : π (Sum.inl r₁) = Sum.inr a) (hp₁ : π (Sum.inr r₁) = D.val (Sum.inr a))
    (hb₂ : π (Sum.inl r₂) = Sum.inr b) (hq₂ : π (Sum.inr r₂) = D.val (Sum.inr b))
    (v u : Fin k → l ⊕ l) :
    symplecticActionMatrix R l (D.reconnect (Sum.inr a) (Sum.inr b)) v u =
      -(((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) : R) *
        (Matrix.J l R (v a) (v b) *
          (symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v) (D.val (Sum.inr a)) (D.val (Sum.inr b)) *
            ∏ r ∈ (Finset.univ.erase r₁).erase r₂,
              symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v) (π (Sum.inl r)) (π (Sum.inr r))))) := by
  set p := D.val (Sum.inr a) with hp_def
  set q := D.val (Sum.inr b)
  have hpa : p ≠ Sum.inr a := D.apply_ne (Sum.inr a)
  have hqb : q ≠ Sum.inr b := D.apply_ne (Sum.inr b)
  have hpq : p ≠ q := fun h => Sum.inr_injective.ne hab (D.val.injective h)
  set W₀ := symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v)
  have hr₁_mem : r₁ ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin k)) := Finset.mem_univ r₁
  have hr₂_mem : r₂ ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin k)).erase r₁ :=
    Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨hr.symm, Finset.mem_univ r₂⟩
  rw [symplecticActionMatrix_apply, signedWeight_reconnect (symplecticArcWeight_swap R l _) D hcup,
    ← hp_def, signedWeight_eq_of_congr_permToBrauer_one
      (fun x y => symplecticArcWeight_swap R l _ _ _) hD,
    zsmul_eq_mul, ← Finset.mul_prod_erase Finset.univ _ hr₁_mem,
    ← Finset.mul_prod_erase (Finset.univ.erase r₁) _ hr₂_mem, ha₁, hp₁, hb₂, hq₂]
  have h₁ : W₀ (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (Sum.inr a)) (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) p) =
      Matrix.J l R (v a) (v b) := by
    rw [Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne hpa.symm (Sum.inr_injective.ne hab), Equiv.swap_apply_left]
    rfl
  have h₂ : W₀ (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (Sum.inr b)) (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) q) = W₀ p q := by
    rw [Equiv.swap_apply_right, Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne hpq.symm hqb]
  have hP : (∏ r ∈ (Finset.univ.erase r₁).erase r₂,
      W₀ (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (π (Sum.inl r)))
         (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (π (Sum.inr r)))) =
      ∏ r ∈ (Finset.univ.erase r₁).erase r₂, W₀ (π (Sum.inl r)) (π (Sum.inr r)) := by
    refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun r hmem => ?_
    obtain ⟨hrr₂, hrr₁'⟩ := Finset.mem_erase.mp hmem
    have hrr₁ : r ≠ r₁ := (Finset.mem_erase.mp hrr₁').1
    have hinl : Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (π (Sum.inl r)) = π (Sum.inl r) :=
      Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne
        (fun h => Sum.inl_ne_inr (π.injective (h.trans hp₁.symm)))
        (fun h => hrr₂ (Sum.inl_injective (π.injective (h.trans hb₂.symm))))
    have hinr : Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (π (Sum.inr r)) = π (Sum.inr r) :=
      Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne
        (fun h => hrr₁ (Sum.inr_injective (π.injective (h.trans hp₁.symm))))
        (fun h => Sum.inr_ne_inl (π.injective (h.trans hb₂.symm)))
    rw [hinl, hinr]
  -- Fold `W₀` on the left so `h₁`, `h₂` and `hP` match directly.
  change -(((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) : R) *
    (W₀ (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (Sum.inr a)) (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) p) *
      (W₀ (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (Sum.inr b)) (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) q) *
        ∏ r ∈ (Finset.univ.erase r₁).erase r₂,
          W₀ (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (π (Sum.inl r)))
             (Equiv.swap p (Sum.inr b) (π (Sum.inr r)))))) = _
  rw [h₁, h₂, hP]

/-- When `D` does not cup `a` to `b`, multiplying `(capCup a b).symplecticActionMatrix` by
`D.symplecticActionMatrix` gives the matrix of `D.reconnect (Sum.inr a) (Sum.inr b)`. -/
private theorem symplecticActionMatrix_capCup_mul_of_not_cup {a b : Fin k} (hab : a ≠ b)
    {D : BrauerDiagram k} (hcup : D.val (Sum.inr a) ≠ Sum.inr b) (v u : Fin k → l ⊕ l) :
    ((capCup a b).symplecticActionMatrix R l * D.symplecticActionMatrix R l) v u =
      symplecticActionMatrix R l (D.reconnect (Sum.inr a) (Sum.inr b)) v u := by
  set p := D.val (Sum.inr a) with hp_def
  set q := D.val (Sum.inr b) with hq_def
  have hpa : p ≠ Sum.inr a := D.apply_ne (Sum.inr a)
  have hqa : q ≠ Sum.inr a := fun h => hcup (D.apply_eq_of_apply_eq h)
  have hqb : q ≠ Sum.inr b := D.apply_ne (Sum.inr b)
  obtain ⟨r₁, r₂, π, hr, hD, ha₁, hp₁, hb₂, hq₂⟩ :=
    exists_congr_permToBrauer_one_of_val_ne D (Sum.inr_injective.ne hab) hcup
  have hrec := symplecticActionMatrix_reconnect_inr_eq R l hab hcup hr hD ha₁ hp₁ hb₂ hq₂ v u
  rw [← hp_def] at hp₁ hrec
  rw [← hq_def] at hq₂ hrec
  set W₀ := symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u v) with hW₀_def
  set P : R := ∏ r ∈ (Finset.univ.erase r₁).erase r₂, W₀ (π (Sum.inl r)) (π (Sum.inr r))
  have hr₁_mem : r₁ ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin k)) := Finset.mem_univ r₁
  have hr₂_mem : r₂ ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin k)).erase r₁ :=
    Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨hr.symm, Finset.mem_univ r₂⟩
  have hrest (x y : l ⊕ l) :
      D.signedWeight
        (symplecticArcWeight R l (Sum.elim u (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y))) =
        ((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) : R) *
          (symplecticArcWeight R l
            (Sum.elim u (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y)) (Sum.inr a) p *
           (symplecticArcWeight R l
            (Sum.elim u (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y)) (Sum.inr b) q * P)) := by
    rw [signedWeight_eq_of_congr_permToBrauer_one (symplecticArcWeight_swap R l _) hD, zsmul_eq_mul,
      ← Finset.mul_prod_erase Finset.univ _ hr₁_mem,
      ← Finset.mul_prod_erase (Finset.univ.erase r₁) _ hr₂_mem, ha₁, hp₁, hb₂, hq₂]
    refine congrArg (fun t : R => ((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) : R) * (_ * (_ * t)))
      (Finset.prod_congr rfl fun r hmem => ?_)
    obtain ⟨hrr₂, hrr₁'⟩ := Finset.mem_erase.mp hmem
    have hrr₁ : r ≠ r₁ := (Finset.mem_erase.mp hrr₁').1
    exact symplecticArcWeight_congr R l
      (sum_elim_update_inr_of_ne l u v x y
        (fun h => Sum.inl_injective.ne hrr₁ (π.injective (h.trans ha₁.symm)))
        (fun h => Sum.inl_injective.ne hrr₂ (π.injective (h.trans hb₂.symm))))
      (sum_elim_update_inr_of_ne l u v x y
        (fun h => Sum.inr_ne_inl (π.injective (h.trans ha₁.symm)))
        (fun h => Sum.inr_ne_inl (π.injective (h.trans hb₂.symm))))
  rw [Matrix.mul_apply, sum_capCup_mul_eq R l hab, hrec]
  simp_rw [symplecticActionMatrix_apply, hrest]
  have hpull : (∑ x : l ⊕ l, ∑ y : l ⊕ l,
      Matrix.J l R x y *
        (((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) : R) *
          (symplecticArcWeight R l
            (Sum.elim u (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y)) (Sum.inr a) p *
           (symplecticArcWeight R l
            (Sum.elim u (Function.update (Function.update v a x) b y)) (Sum.inr b) q * P)))) =
      ((Equiv.Perm.sign π : ℤ) : R) * (W₀ p q * P) := by
    rw [hW₀_def, ← sum_J_mul_symplecticArcWeight_mul R l hab v u hpa hcup hqa hqb]
    symm
    rw [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => ?_
    rw [Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => by ring
  rw [hpull]
  ring

/-- Multiplying on the left by a cap-cup generator satisfies the symplectic loop rule. -/
private theorem symplecticActionMatrix_capCup_mul {a b : Fin k} (hab : a ≠ b)
    (D : BrauerDiagram k) :
    (capCup a b).symplecticActionMatrix R l * D.symplecticActionMatrix R l =
      (-(2 * Fintype.card l : R)) ^ middleLoopCount (capCup a b) D •
        (composeDiagram (capCup a b) D).symplecticActionMatrix R l := by
  ext v u
  rw [middleLoopCount_capCup_left hab, composeDiagram_capCup_left hab]
  split_ifs with hcup
  · rw [pow_one, Matrix.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul,
      symplecticActionMatrix_capCup_mul_of_cup R l hab hcup]
    congr 2
    rw [← hcup, PerfectMatching.reconnect_partner]
  · rw [pow_zero, one_smul, symplecticActionMatrix_capCup_mul_of_not_cup R l hab hcup]

/-- **The symplectic loop rule for the matrices of Brauer diagrams.** The matrix of `D₁` times the
matrix of `D₂` is the matrix of `TauCeti.composeDiagram D₁ D₂`, scaled by `(-2|l|)` to the number of
closed middle loops. -/
theorem symplecticActionMatrix_mul (D₁ D₂ : BrauerDiagram k) :
    D₁.symplecticActionMatrix R l * D₂.symplecticActionMatrix R l =
      (-(2 * Fintype.card l : R)) ^ middleLoopCount D₁ D₂ •
        (composeDiagram D₁ D₂).symplecticActionMatrix R l := by
  induction D₁ using BrauerDiagram.capCup_induction_on with
  | permToBrauer σ =>
    rw [middleLoopCount_permToBrauer_left, pow_zero, one_smul,
      symplecticActionMatrix_permToBrauer_mul]
  | capCup_compose a b X hab hloop ih =>
    have hX := symplecticActionMatrix_capCup_mul R l hab X
    rw [hloop, pow_zero, one_smul] at hX
    have hloop_assoc :
        middleLoopCount X D₂ + middleLoopCount (capCup a b) (composeDiagram X D₂) =
          middleLoopCount (composeDiagram (capCup a b) X) D₂ := by
      have h := (middleLoopCount_add_middleLoopCount_composeDiagram (capCup a b) X D₂).symm
      rwa [hloop, zero_add] at h
    rw [← hX, Matrix.mul_assoc, ih, Matrix.mul_smul, symplecticActionMatrix_capCup_mul R l hab,
      smul_smul, ← pow_add, hloop_assoc, ← composeDiagram_assoc]

end Mul

end BrauerDiagram

/-! ### Monomial basis and group-algebra action on the symplectic tensor power -/

section SymplecticAction

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (n k : ℕ)

/-- **The monomial basis of `((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)^{⊗k}`**: the basis vector at
`f : Fin k → Fin n ⊕ Fin n` is the pure tensor whose `i`-th factor is the `f i`-th standard basis
vector of `(Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R`. -/
noncomputable def symplecticTensorPowerBasis :
    Module.Basis (Fin k → Fin n ⊕ Fin n) R (⨂[R]^k ((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)) :=
  Basis.piTensorProduct fun _ : Fin k => Pi.basisFun R (Fin n ⊕ Fin n)

theorem symplecticTensorPowerBasis_def :
    symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k =
      Basis.piTensorProduct fun _ : Fin k => Pi.basisFun R (Fin n ⊕ Fin n) :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem symplecticTensorPowerBasis_apply (f : Fin k → Fin n ⊕ Fin n) :
    symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k f =
      PiTensorProduct.tprod R fun i => Pi.single (f i) (1 : R) := by
  classical
  rw [symplecticTensorPowerBasis, Basis.piTensorProduct_apply]
  simp

/-- **The dimension of `((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)^{⊗k}` is `(2 * n) ^ k`.** -/
theorem finrank_symplecticTensorPower [StrongRankCondition R] :
    Module.finrank R (⨂[R]^k ((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)) = (2 * n) ^ k := by
  simp [Module.finrank_eq_card_basis (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k), two_mul]

/-- **The matrix of `A^{⊗k}` in `symplecticTensorPowerBasis` is `A.kroneckerPower (Fin k)`.** -/
theorem _root_.Matrix.toMatrix_piTensorProductMap_symplecticTensorPowerBasis {R : Type u}
    [CommRing R] {n k : ℕ} (A : Matrix (Fin n ⊕ Fin n) (Fin n ⊕ Fin n) R) :
    LinearMap.toMatrix (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k) (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k)
        (PiTensorProduct.map fun _ : Fin k => A.mulVecLin) =
      A.kroneckerPower (Fin k) := by
  rw [symplecticTensorPowerBasis_def]
  exact A.toMatrix_piTensorProductMap_mulVecLin

/-- A permutation acts on the monomial basis of `((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)^{⊗k}` by precomposing the
index function with its inverse and scaling by `sign σ`. -/
theorem symplecticPermTensorAction_symplecticTensorPowerBasis (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin k))
    (f : Fin k → Fin n ⊕ Fin n) :
    symplecticPermTensorAction R n k σ (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k f) =
      ((Equiv.Perm.sign σ : ℤ) : R) •
        symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k fun i => f (σ.symm i) := by
  simp

/-- **The sign-twisted group-algebra action** of `R[S_k]` on `((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)^{⊗k}`, extending
`TauCeti.symplecticPermTensorAction`. -/
noncomputable def symplecticPermTensorActionAlgHom :
    MonoidAlgebra R (Equiv.Perm (Fin k)) →ₐ[R]
      Module.End R (⨂[R]^k ((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)) :=
  (symplecticPermTensorAction R n k).asAlgebraHom

theorem symplecticPermTensorActionAlgHom_def :
    symplecticPermTensorActionAlgHom R n k = (symplecticPermTensorAction R n k).asAlgebraHom :=
  (rfl)

theorem symplecticPermTensorActionAlgHom_of (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin k)) :
    symplecticPermTensorActionAlgHom R n k (MonoidAlgebra.of R (Equiv.Perm (Fin k)) σ) =
      symplecticPermTensorAction R n k σ := by
  rw [symplecticPermTensorActionAlgHom_def, Representation.asAlgebraHom_of]

/-! ### The symplectic Brauer algebra action -/

/-- **The Brauer algebra acting on a tensor power of the standard symplectic module.** The Brauer
algebra `B_k(-2n)` at the loop value `-2n = -dim R^{2n}` acts on `((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)^{⊗k}`
through the standard alternating form: a diagram acts by
`TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix` in `TauCeti.symplecticTensorPowerBasis`, and these
matrices obey the loop rule (`TauCeti.BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix_mul`). -/
noncomputable def brauerActionSymp :
    BrauerAlgebra R (-(2 * n : R)) k →ₐ[R]
      Module.End R (⨂[R]^k ((Fin n ⊕ Fin n) → R)) :=
  BrauerAlgebra.lift
    (fun D => Matrix.toLin (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k) (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k)
      (D.symplecticActionMatrix R (Fin n)))
    (by
      rw [BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix_permToBrauer_one, Matrix.toLin_one,
        Module.End.one_eq_id])
    fun D₁ D₂ => by
      rw [Module.End.mul_eq_comp, ← Matrix.toLin_mul, BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix_mul,
        Fintype.card_fin, map_smul]

/-- A Brauer diagram acts by its symplectic action matrix in `symplecticTensorPowerBasis`. -/
theorem brauerActionSymp_of (D : BrauerDiagram k) :
    brauerActionSymp R n k (BrauerAlgebra.of D) =
      Matrix.toLin (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k) (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k)
        (D.symplecticActionMatrix R (Fin n)) :=
  BrauerAlgebra.lift_of ..

/-- **The matrix of the symplectic Brauer action.** In `symplecticTensorPowerBasis`, an element `x`
of `B_k(-2n)` acts by the combination `∑ D, x.coeff D • M(D)` of the symplectic diagram matrices. -/
theorem toMatrix_brauerActionSymp (x : BrauerAlgebra R (-(2 * n : R)) k) :
    LinearMap.toMatrix (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k) (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k)
        (brauerActionSymp R n k x) =
      Finsupp.linearCombination R
        (fun D : BrauerDiagram k => D.symplecticActionMatrix R (Fin n)) x.coeff := by
  have h : (LinearMap.toMatrix (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k)
          (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k)).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        (brauerActionSymp R n k).toLinearMap =
      Finsupp.linearCombination R
          (fun D : BrauerDiagram k => D.symplecticActionMatrix R (Fin n)) ∘ₗ
        (BrauerAlgebra.coeffLinearEquiv R (-(2 * n : R)) k).toLinearMap :=
    (BrauerAlgebra.basis R (-(2 * n : R)) k).ext fun D => by
      simp [BrauerAlgebra.basis_apply, brauerActionSymp_of, BrauerAlgebra.coeffLinearEquiv_apply]
  simpa using LinearMap.congr_fun h x

/-- **A Brauer diagram on a monomial basis tensor.** -/
theorem brauerActionSymp_of_symplecticTensorPowerBasis (D : BrauerDiagram k)
    (u : Fin k → Fin n ⊕ Fin n) :
    brauerActionSymp R n k (BrauerAlgebra.of D) (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k u) =
      ∑ v, D.symplecticActionMatrix R (Fin n) v u • symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k v := by
  rw [brauerActionSymp_of, Matrix.toLin_self]

/-- **Permutation diagrams act by the sign-twisted permutation action.** -/
@[simp]
theorem brauerActionSymp_of_permToBrauer (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin k)) :
    brauerActionSymp R n k (BrauerAlgebra.of (permToBrauer σ)) =
      symplecticPermTensorAction R n k σ := by
  refine (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k).ext fun u => ?_
  rw [brauerActionSymp_of_symplecticTensorPowerBasis,
    symplecticPermTensorAction_symplecticTensorPowerBasis,
    Finset.sum_eq_single (fun i => u (σ.symm i))]
  · rw [BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix_permToBrauer]
    simp
  · intro v _ hv
    rw [BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix_permToBrauer]
    simp [hv]
  · simp

/-- **The symplectic Brauer action restricts along `ofPerm` to the sign-twisted group-algebra
action.** -/
theorem brauerActionSymp_comp_ofPerm :
    (brauerActionSymp R n k).comp (BrauerAlgebra.ofPerm R (-(2 * n : R)) k) =
      symplecticPermTensorActionAlgHom R n k := by
  refine MonoidAlgebra.algHom_ext (fun σ => ?_) (by ext)
  rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, BrauerAlgebra.ofPerm_single, map_smul, one_smul,
    brauerActionSymp_of_permToBrauer, ← symplecticPermTensorActionAlgHom_of, MonoidAlgebra.of_apply]

/-- **Cap-cup diagrams act by the single-arc generators `symplecticCupCapAt`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem brauerActionSymp_of_capCup {a b : Fin k} (hab : a ≠ b) :
    brauerActionSymp R n k (BrauerAlgebra.of (capCup a b)) = symplecticCupCapAt R n k a b := by
  apply (LinearMap.toMatrix (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k)
    (symplecticTensorPowerBasis R n k)).injective
  ext v u
  rw [brauerActionSymp_of, LinearMap.toMatrix_toLin, BrauerDiagram.symplecticActionMatrix_capCup
    R (Fin n) hab, LinearMap.toMatrix_apply, symplecticTensorPowerBasis_def]
  exact (piTensorProduct_repr_symplecticCupCapAt_piTensorProduct hab u v).symm

/-- **The image of `B_k(-2n)` is generated by the sign-twisted permutations and one symplectic
cap-cup operator.** -/
theorem range_brauerActionSymp_eq_adjoin {a b : Fin k} (hab : a ≠ b) :
    (brauerActionSymp R n k).range =
      Algebra.adjoin R
        (insert (symplecticCupCapAt R n k a b) (Set.range (symplecticPermTensorAction R n k))) := by
  rw [← Algebra.map_top,
    ← BrauerAlgebra.adjoin_insert_of_capCup_range_of_permToBrauer R (-(2 * n : R)) hab,
    AlgHom.map_adjoin, Set.image_insert_eq, ← Set.range_comp, brauerActionSymp_of_capCup R n k hab]
  simp only [Function.comp_def, brauerActionSymp_of_permToBrauer]

end SymplecticAction

